      "title": "Think-Aloud SLM: reasoning silence vs speech overhang",
      "kind": "facets",
      "note": "Table 3, v1; Spoken-MQA. Lsil is cumulative silence while reasoning continues; Loh is extra delay when progress speech outlasts answer readiness. Neither is first-audio or first-correct-answer latency. An active utterance finishes before final-response generation; only pending unsynthesized updates are canceled. Rates denote reasoning generation, not a shared hardware test. Source dashes stay NR. No implemented interruption test.",
      "takeaway": "At 40 tok/s, dynamic balance reduces cumulative reasoning silence from 12.82 s for serial CoT to 0.36 s, but adds 4.34 s speech overhang. Raising generation speed further reduces silence while overhang is non-monotonic. Masked silence is not evidence of an earlier correct answer.",
